    <item>
      <title>Introduction</title>
      <link>https://nmusers.github.io/docs/user-guide/introduction/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://nmusers.github.io/docs/user-guide/introduction/</guid>
      <description>&lt;link rel=&#34;stylesheet&#34; href=&#34;https://nmusers.github.io/docs/katex/katex.min.css&#34; /&gt;&lt;script defer src=&#34;https://nmusers.github.io/docs/katex/katex.min.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&lt;script defer src=&#34;https://nmusers.github.io/docs/katex/auto-render.min.js&#34; onload=&#34;renderMathInElement(document.body, {&amp;#34;delimiters&amp;#34;:[{&amp;#34;left&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;$$&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;right&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;$$&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;display&amp;#34;:true},{&amp;#34;left&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\(&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;right&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\)&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;display&amp;#34;:false},{&amp;#34;left&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\[&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;right&amp;#34;:&amp;#34;\\]&amp;#34;,&amp;#34;display&amp;#34;:true}]});&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;outline-container-headline-1&#34; class=&#34;outline-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;headline-1&#34;&gt;&#xA;Introduction&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div id=&#34;outline-text-headline-1&#34; class=&#34;outline-text-2&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;NONMEM stands for &amp;#34;Nonlinear Mixed Effects Model.&amp;#34; Written in Fortran&#xA;90/95, NONMEM fits general nonlinear regression-type models to data.&#xA;The data are typically collected from clinical studies of pharmaceutic&#xA;agents, involving the administration of a drug to individuals and the&#xA;subsequent observation of drug levels (most often in the blood&#xA;plasma). Proper modeling of these data involves accounting for both&#xA;inter- and intra-subject effects (random effects), as well as measured&#xA;concomitant effects (fixed effects). This mixed effect modeling&#xA;approach, and the nonlinear nature of the biochemical and&#xA;physiological process involved, is the bedrock of NONMEM. Such&#xA;modeling is especially useful when there are only a few&#xA;pharmacokinetic measurements from each individual sampled in the&#xA;population, or when the data collection design varies considerably&#xA;between these individuals. However, NONMEM is a general program which&#xA;can be used to fit models to a wide variety of data.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
